t during his reign. The Al-Mu'izz Street in Cairo is named after him, it is considered to be the most important historical street in Cairo and it includes monumental buildings from the Fatimid era as well as the later Ayyubid, Memluk and Ottoman eras.","wp_description":"Fatimid caliph from 953 to 975","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Mu%27izz_li-Din_Allah","image_lead":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d7/Fatimiden-_Abu_Tamim_al-Muizz_-_M%C3%BCnzkabinett%2C_Berlin_-_5545286.jpg","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Fatimiden-_Abu_Tamim_al-Muizz_-_M%C3%BCnzkabinett%2C_Berlin_-_5545286.jpg/960px-Fatimiden-_Abu_Tamim_al-Muizz_-_M%C3%BCnzkabinett%2C_Berlin_-_5545286.jpg","chat_ready":true,"display_from":953,"display_to":975}